---
import DocsLayout from "~/layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
---
<DocsLayout
  active="api"
  title="HTTP API"
  description="Put Redax directly in front of your LLM call. Send text in, receive safe text plus the evidence you need to operate the boundary."
>
  <section class="card border-flame-400/20 bg-flame-500/[0.06] p-6 sm:p-8">
    <div class="text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-flame-300">Why this endpoint exists</div>
    <p class="mt-4 text-[16px] leading-[1.7] text-ink-100">An LLM provider should never be the first system that sees customer text. <code>/v1/redact</code> gives your application one explicit boundary: the raw request enters Redax, sensitive spans are replaced locally, and only the safe result continues to the model.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-[25px] text-ink-0">The request path</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">Call this endpoint before your model call. The steps are intentionally visible so a developer can reason about privacy, correctness, and operations separately.</p>
    <div class="mt-5 grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-2">
      {[ ["1", "Send", "Your application sends text and an optional policy."], ["2", "Detect", "Regex and/or a local NER model find candidate spans."], ["3", "Replace", "Redax applies the policy and creates typed placeholders."], ["4", "Continue", "Your model receives only the redacted text."] ].map(([n, title, body]) => (
        <div class="card p-4"><div class="font-mono text-[11px] text-flame-300">{n}</div><div class="mt-3 text-[14px] font-semibold text-ink-0">{title}</div><div class="mt-1 text-[12px] leading-[1.5] text-ink-400">{body}</div></div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-[25px] text-ink-0">Start with one request</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">The smallest useful integration is one JSON request. Authentication is optional in local development and enabled with <code>X-API-Key</code> in a deployed environment.</p>
    <pre class="code-shell mt-5 overflow-x-auto p-5 text-[13px] leading-[1.7] text-ink-100"><code>{`curl -s -X POST http://localhost:8000/v1/redact \\
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\
  -H 'X-Request-ID: checkout-8421' \\
  -d '{"text":"Email me at alice@example.com"}'`}</code></pre>
    <p class="mt-3 text-[13.5px] text-ink-400">Use <code>X-Request-ID</code> to correlate the response, application logs, traces, and audit event. Redax echoes it back.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-[25px] text-ink-0">Request fields</h2>
    <div class="mt-4 grid gap-3">
      {[ ["text", "required", "The string to inspect. The maximum is controlled by REDAX_MAX_TEXT_CHARS."], ["entity_types", "optional", "Limit detection to types such as email, person, phone, or SSN_US."], ["policy", "optional", "Inline policy override. Omit it to use REDAX_DEFAULT_POLICY."], ["use_pipeline", "optional", "Route through the staged regex/model/consensus pipeline. Leave unset for the legacy Redactor path when you need policy relexicalization."] ].map(([name, status, body]) => (
        <div class="card p-5 sm:grid sm:grid-cols-[150px_90px_1fr] sm:gap-4 sm:items-start"><code class="text-flame-200">{name}</code><span class="mt-1 sm:mt-0 text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-ink-500">{status}</span><p class="mt-2 sm:mt-0 text-[14px] text-ink-300">{body}</p></div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-[25px] text-ink-0">Response shape</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">The response serves two consumers: the next LLM call needs <code>text</code>, while your application and operators need spans, a digest, and pipeline state. The audit log records metadata, never the original value.</p>
    <pre class="code-shell mt-5 overflow-x-auto p-5 text-[13px] leading-[1.7] text-ink-100"><code>{`{
  "text": "Email me at [EMAIL_0000]",
  "spans": [{"start": 12, "end": 29, "type": "EMAIL", "confidence": 1.0}],
  "relex_map": {},
  "used_pipeline": false,
  "used_fallback": false,
  "digest": "8f1d2c..."
}`}</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-[25px] text-ink-0">Choose the endpoint for the workload</h2>
    <div class="mt-4 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
      {[ ["/v1/redact", "One request", "Interactive prompts, chat messages, and synchronous API calls."], ["/v1/redact/batch", "Many requests", "Up to 1,000 items in parallel under one overall timeout."], ["/v1/redact/stream", "Long documents", "Server-sent events for chunked processing without waiting for the whole document."], ["/v1/jobs", "Async work", "Queue large jobs, poll by ID, and keep the request thread responsive."] ].map(([path, title, body]) => (
        <div class="card p-5"><code class="text-flame-200">{path}</code><div class="mt-3 text-[15px] font-semibold text-ink-0">{title}</div><p class="mt-1.5 text-[13.5px] text-ink-400">{body}</p></div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-[25px] text-ink-0">Errors and safe retries</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">Errors use RFC 7807 <code>application/problem+json</code> so clients can branch on stable status and type fields. Expect <code>413</code> for oversized input, <code>422</code> for invalid JSON, <code>429</code> for rate limits, <code>503</code> when the service is not ready, and <code>504</code> for a timeout.</p>
    <p class="mt-3">Send an <code>Idempotency-Key</code> with retryable POST requests. Redax returns the same result for the same key instead of performing duplicate work, which matters when a queue or load balancer retries after a network interruption.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="card p-6 sm:p-8">
    <h2 class="text-[22px] text-ink-0">Next step</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">Once the single request works, read the integration guide to place Redax before and after the model call, then use the deployment checklist before exposing it to production traffic.</p>
    <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-3"><a href="/redax/docs/integration" class="btn-primary">Read integration →</a><a href="/redax/docs/deployment" class="btn-ghost">Production checklist</a></div>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
